      "commit": {
        "author": "\"Zach Aller\" <code@example.com>",
        "date": "2026-10-13T15:04:30-05:00",
        "subject": "test: track the externally closed PR by UID, not name (#2288)",
        "body": "\"should remove CTP finalizer from PR when PR is externally closed\" waited\nfor the PullRequest name to return NotFound. The CTP still has a pending\npromotion, so once the closed PR is gone it creates a new one with the\nsame name, often within ~10ms. The spec passed only when a poll landed in\nthat gap and timed out otherwise (about 1 run in 5 locally).\n\nRecord the closed PR's UID, delete with a UID precondition, and pass once\nno PullRequest with that UID exists.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KMbKRJK45xAEBq9tQoc9DG\n\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "sha": "b7adbd8aaf79df3ee147b0385094dda9defed4d3",
        "repoUrl": "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/gitops-promoter"
      }
    }
  ]
}
